IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-accounts.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 4 (annual accounts), General and Individual accounts, ss 393 to 398
-- (lines 5044-5142 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Duties that apply only on a condition are encoded as "is required" (JUST TRUE where the duty applies, JUST FALSE where the text's own
-- wording takes it away); duties that list contents are encoded over the facts a witness can state. Section 398 is blank in this text.

§ `Chapter 4: Annual accounts`

§§ `General: accounts to give true and fair view`

-- ---- s 393 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5047 | (1) The directors of a company must not approve accounts for the purposes of this Chapter unless they are satisfied that they give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss—
-- src:5048 | (a) in the case of the company's individual accounts, of the company;
@ref s 393(1)(a) The directors' condition for approving individual accounts (src:5047-5048)
GIVEN `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1)(a) the condition for approving the company's individual accounts is met` MEANS
    IF `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a company must not approve accounts for the purposes of this Chapter unless they are satisfied that they give a true and fair view"

-- src:5047 | (1) The directors of a company must not approve accounts for the purposes of this Chapter unless they are satisfied that they give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss—
-- src:5048 | (a) in the case of the company's individual accounts, of the company;
-- src:5049 | (b) in the case of the company's group accounts, of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company.
@ref s 393(1)(b) The directors' condition for approving group accounts (src:5047-5049)
GIVEN `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1)(b) the condition for approving the company's group accounts is met` MEANS
    IF `the directors are satisfied that the accounts give a true and fair view of the assets, liabilities, financial position and profit or loss of the undertakings included in the consolidation as a whole, so far as concerns members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a company must not approve accounts for the purposes of this Chapter unless they are satisfied that they give a true and fair view"

-- src:5050 | (2) The auditor of a company in carrying out his functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts must have regard to the directors' duty under subsection (1).
@ref s 393(2) The auditor must have regard to the directors' duty (src:5050)
GIVEN `the auditor is carrying out functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(2) the auditor is required to have regard to the directors' duty under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the auditor is carrying out functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in carrying out his functions under this Act in relation to the company's annual accounts"

-- src:5051 | (1A) The following provisions apply to the directors of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year (see sections 384A and 384B) in their consideration of whether the Companies Act individual accounts of the company for that year give a true and fair view as required by subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:5052 | (a) where the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items,
-- src:5053 | (b) in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to that item, and
-- src:5054 | (c) where the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must have regard to any provision of an accounting standard which relates to that item.
@ref s 393(1A) Micro-entities: the directors' consideration of the true and fair view (src:5051-5054)
GIVEN `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1A)(a) the directors must disregard an accounting standard provision requiring information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items` MEANS
    IF `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` AND `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` AND `the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items"

-- src:5051 | (1A) The following provisions apply to the directors of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to a financial year (see sections 384A and 384B) in their consideration of whether the Companies Act individual accounts of the company for that year give a true and fair view as required by subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:5052 | (a) where the accounts comprise only micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain information additional to those items,
-- src:5053 | (b) in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to that item, and
@ref s 393(1A)(b) Micro-entities: a micro-entity minimum accounting item (src:5051-5053)
GIVEN `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item is a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1A)(b) the directors must disregard an accounting standard provision requiring further information in relation to the item` MEANS
    IF `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` AND `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` AND `the item is a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a micro-entity minimum accounting item contained in the accounts, the directors must disregard any provision of an accounting standard which would require the accounts to contain further information in relation to that item"

-- src:5054 | (c) where the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must have regard to any provision of an accounting standard which relates to that item.
@ref s 393(1A)(c) Micro-entities: additional items (src:5054)
GIVEN `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1A)(c) the directors must have regard to an accounting standard provision relating to the additional item` MEANS
    IF `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` AND `the accounts are the Companies Act individual accounts of the company` AND `the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accounts contain an item of information additional to the micro-entity minimum accounting items, the directors must have regard to any provision of an accounting standard which relates to that item"

§§ `Individual accounts`

-- ---- s 394: duty to prepare individual accounts -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5057 | The directors of every company must prepare accounts for the company for each of its financial years unless the company is exempt from that requirement under section 394A.
@ref s 394 Duty to prepare individual accounts (src:5057)
GIVEN `s 394A the company is exempt from the requirement under section 394A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394 the directors are required to prepare individual accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the company is exempt from that requirement under section 394A"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the section 394A answer is not known
    `s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 394A the company is exempt from the requirement under section 394A`

-- src:5058 | Those accounts are referred to as the company's “individual accounts”.
@ref s 394 "individual accounts" (src:5058)
GIVEN `the accounts were prepared by the directors of the company under section 394` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394 the accounts are the company's individual accounts` MEANS
    IF `the accounts were prepared by the directors of the company under section 394`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Those accounts are referred to as the company's “individual accounts”" (IAS individual accounts under section 395 are also individual accounts)

-- ---- s 394A: dormant subsidiaries exemption ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5060 | (1) A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts for a financial year if—
-- src:5061 | (a) it is itself a subsidiary undertaking,
-- src:5062 | (b) it has been dormant throughout the whole of that year, and
-- src:5063 | (c) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 394A(1) Exemption for dormant subsidiaries (src:5060-5063)
GIVEN `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394A(1) the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts for a financial year if (a) it is itself a subsidiary undertaking, (b) it has been dormant throughout the whole of that year, and (c) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the subsidiary undertaking answer (section 1162) is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking`
        (JUST (`s 1169(1) the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the year` AND `its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`))

-- src:5084 | 394C Dormant subsidiaries exemption: parent undertaking declaration of guarantee
-- src:5085 | (1) A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section.
@ref s 394C(1) A guarantee is given when the directors deliver the parent undertaking's statement (src:5084-5085)
GIVEN `the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement"

-- src:5064 | (2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions—
-- src:5065 | (a) all members of the company must agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question,
-- src:5066 | (b) the parent undertaking must give a guarantee under section 394C in respect of that year,
-- src:5067 | (c) the company must be included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with—
-- src:5068 | (i) if the undertaking is a company, the requirements of this Part of this Act, or, if the undertaking is not a company, the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking, or
-- src:5069 | (ii) UK-adopted international accounting standards,
-- src:5070 | (d) the parent undertaking must disclose in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of this section, and
-- src:5071 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar within the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year—
-- src:5072 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:5073 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 394C(1),
-- src:5074 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:5075 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:5076 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 394A(2) The conditions of the exemption (src:5064-5076)
-- "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions". The period for filing is section 442 (coa10): an input date.
GIVEN `all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking in respect of that year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with the requirements of this Part or the legal requirements that apply to it, or UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of section 394A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar the statement referred to in section 394C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the directors delivered the documents` IS A DATE
      `s 442 the last day of the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394A(2) the conditions of the exemption are all complied with` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the guarantee answer (section 394C) is not known and no other condition fails
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST (`all members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question`
                                        AND `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with the requirements of this Part or the legal requirements that apply to it, or UK-adopted international accounting standards`
                                        AND `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the company is exempt from the requirement to prepare individual accounts by virtue of section 394A`
                                        AND `the directors have delivered to the registrar a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a)`
                                        AND `the directors have delivered to the registrar the statement referred to in section 394C(1)`
                                        AND `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c)`
                                        AND `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts`
                                        AND `the directors have delivered to the registrar a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking`
                                        AND `the date on which the directors delivered the documents` AT MOST `s 442 the last day of the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year`))
                                `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking in respect of that year`

-- src:5078 | A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A (dormant subsidiaries) if it was at any time within the financial year in question—
-- src:5079 | (a) a traded company,
-- src:5080 | (b) a company that—
-- src:5081 | (i) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:5082 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:5083 | (c) a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (c 52) or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 ( S.I. 1992/807) ( NI 5).
@ref s 394B Companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption (src:5078-5083)
GIVEN `s 360C the company was at any time within the financial year a traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1165(2) the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1164(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company was at any time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394B the company is entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A` MEANS
    CONSIDER excluded
    WHEN JUST isExcluded THEN
        IF isExcluded
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not entitled to the exemption conferred by section 394A (dormant subsidiaries) if it was at any time within the financial year in question"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 394B only withholds the exemption; section 394A gives it
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a borrowed answer is not known and no limb decides
    WHERE
        excluded MEANS
            `s 362 helper some answer`
                (LIST `s 360C the company was at any time within the financial year a traded company`,
                      JUST `s 1165(2) the company was at any time within the financial year an authorised insurance company`,
                      JUST `s 1164(2) the company was at any time within the financial year a banking company`,
                      `the company was at any time within the financial year an e-money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company`,
                      `the company at any time within the financial year carried on insurance market activity`,
                      `the company was at any time within the financial year a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`)

-- ---- s 394C: dormant subsidiaries exemption: parent undertaking declaration of guarantee -------------------------------------------

-- src:5086 | (2) The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify—
-- src:5087 | (a) the name of the parent undertaking,
-- src:5088 | (b) the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking,
-- src:5089 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:5090 | (d) the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given,
-- src:5091 | (e) the date of the statement, and
-- src:5092 | (f) the financial year to which the guarantee relates.
@ref s 394C(2) The statement: authentication and contents (src:5086-5092)
-- Paragraph (c) is blank in this text ("..."). The registered number is asked "(if any)".
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394C(2) the statement meets the requirements of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` AND `it specifies the name of the parent undertaking` AND `it specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking` AND `it specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given` AND `it specifies the date of the statement` AND `it specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify"

-- src:5093 | (3) A guarantee given under this section has the effect that—
-- src:5094 | (a) the parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates, until they are satisfied in full, and
@ref s 394C(3)(a) The guarantee covers the outstanding liabilities (src:5093-5094)
GIVEN `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary company is subject to the liability at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability has been satisfied in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394C(3)(a) the parent undertaking guarantees the liability` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A guarantee given under this section has the effect that— (a) the parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates, until they are satisfied in full"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the guarantee answer (subsection (1)) is not known
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` (JUST (`the subsidiary company is subject to the liability at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` AND (NOT `the liability has been satisfied in full`)))

-- src:5095 | (b) the guarantee is enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities.
@ref s 394C(3)(b) The guarantee is enforceable by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable (src:5095)
GIVEN `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394C(3)(b) the person may enforce the guarantee against the parent undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 394C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking`
    WHEN JUST given THEN
        IF NOT given
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A guarantee given under this section has the effect that"
        ELSE IF `the person is a person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- ---- s 395: individual accounts: applicable accounting framework ------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 395(1) accounting framework` IS ONE OF
    `s 395(1)(a) Companies Act individual accounts`
    `s 395(1)(b) IAS individual accounts`

-- src:5101 | (2) The individual accounts of a company that is a charity must be Companies Act individual accounts.
@ref s 395(2) A charity's individual accounts must be Companies Act individual accounts (src:5101)
GIVEN `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(2) the individual accounts must be Companies Act individual accounts` MEANS
    IF `the company is a charity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The individual accounts of a company that is a charity"

-- src:5103 | (4) There is a relevant change of circumstance if, at any time during or after the first IAS year—
-- src:5104 | (a) the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS individual accounts,
-- src:5105 | (aa) the company ceases to be a subsidiary undertaking,
-- src:5106 | (b) the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, or
-- src:5107 | (c) a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
@ref s 395(4) A relevant change of circumstance (src:5103-5107)
GIVEN `the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4) there is a relevant change of circumstance` MEANS
    IF `the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS individual accounts` OR `the company ceases to be a subsidiary undertaking` OR `the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` OR `a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There is a relevant change of circumstance if, at any time during or after the first IAS year"

DECLARE `s 395 earlier change to Companies Act accounts` HAS
    `s 395 the date of the change` IS A DATE
    `s 395 the change was due to a relevant change of circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:5108 | (4A) After a financial year in which the directors of a company prepare IAS individual accounts for the company, the directors may change to preparing Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance provided they have not changed to Companies Act individual accounts in the period of five years preceding the first day of that financial year.
-- src:5109 | (4B) In calculating the five year period for the purpose of subsection (4A), no account should be taken of a change due to a relevant change of circumstance.
@ref s 395(4A) A change to Companies Act individual accounts for another reason; (4B) the five-year period (src:5108-5109)
-- "provided they have not changed to Companies Act individual accounts in the period of five years preceding the first day of that financial year";
-- subsection (4B): a change due to a relevant change of circumstance is not counted.
GIVEN `the first day of the financial year` IS A DATE
      changes IS A LIST OF `s 395 earlier change to Companies Act accounts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(4A) the directors may change to Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 395 the date of the change` AT LEAST `add years` `the first day of the financial year` (-5) AND c's `s 395 the date of the change` LESS THAN `the first day of the financial year` AND (NOT c's `s 395 the change was due to a relevant change of circumstance`)) changes
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided they have not changed to Companies Act individual accounts in the period of five years preceding the first day of that financial year"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5102 | (3) After the first financial year in which the directors of a company prepare IAS individual accounts (“the first IAS year”), all subsequent individual accounts of the company must be prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards unless there is a relevant change of circumstance. This is subject to subsection (4A).
@ref s 395(3) After the first IAS year all subsequent individual accounts must be IAS (src:5102)
GIVEN `the directors have already prepared IAS individual accounts for an earlier financial year (the first IAS year)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 395(4) there is a relevant change of circumstance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors change to Companies Act individual accounts under subsection (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 395(4A) the directors may change to Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(3) the directors must prepare IAS individual accounts for the financial year` MEANS
    IF NOT `the directors have already prepared IAS individual accounts for an earlier financial year (the first IAS year)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the first financial year in which the directors of a company prepare IAS individual accounts"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 395(4) there is a relevant change of circumstance`
         WHEN JUST changed THEN
             IF changed
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless there is a relevant change of circumstance"
             ELSE IF `the directors change to Companies Act individual accounts under subsection (4A)`
                  THEN `s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 395(4A) the directors may change to Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance` -- "This is subject to subsection (4A)"
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5097 | (1) A company's individual accounts may be prepared—
-- src:5098 | (a) in accordance with section 396 (“Companies Act individual accounts”), or
-- src:5099 | (b) in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards (“IAS individual accounts”).
-- src:5100 | This is subject to the following provisions of this section and to section 407 (consistency of financial reporting within group).
-- src:5101 | (2) The individual accounts of a company that is a charity must be Companies Act individual accounts.
-- src:5102 | (3) After the first financial year in which the directors of a company prepare IAS individual accounts (“the first IAS year”), all subsequent individual accounts of the company must be prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards unless there is a relevant change of circumstance. This is subject to subsection (4A).
-- src:5103 | (4) There is a relevant change of circumstance if, at any time during or after the first IAS year—
-- src:5104 | (a) the company becomes a subsidiary undertaking of another undertaking that does not prepare IAS individual accounts,
-- src:5105 | (aa) the company ceases to be a subsidiary undertaking,
-- src:5106 | (b) the company ceases to be a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, or
-- src:5107 | (c) a parent undertaking of the company ceases to be an undertaking with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
-- src:5108 | (4A) After a financial year in which the directors of a company prepare IAS individual accounts for the company, the directors may change to preparing Companies Act individual accounts for a reason other than a relevant change of circumstance provided they have not changed to Companies Act individual accounts in the period of five years preceding the first day of that financial year.
-- src:5109 | (4B) In calculating the five year period for the purpose of subsection (4A), no account should be taken of a change due to a relevant change of circumstance.
-- src:5110 | (5) If, having changed to preparing Companies Act individual accounts . . . , the directors again prepare IAS individual accounts for the company, subsections (3) and (4) apply again as if the first financial year for which such accounts are again prepared were the first IAS year.
@ref s 395(1) Individual accounts: applicable accounting framework (src:5097-5110)
GIVEN framework IS A `s 395(1) accounting framework`
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 395(3) the directors must prepare IAS individual accounts for the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1) the individual accounts may be prepared in accordance with the framework` MEANS
    -- "subject to the following provisions of this section and to section 407": section 407 (consistency within a group) is that section's own answer
    CONSIDER framework
    WHEN `s 395(1)(a) Companies Act individual accounts` THEN `s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 395(3) the directors must prepare IAS individual accounts for the financial year`
    WHEN `s 395(1)(b) IAS individual accounts` THEN
        IF `the company is a charity`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The individual accounts of a company that is a charity must be Companies Act individual accounts"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5110 | (5) If, having changed to preparing Companies Act individual accounts . . . , the directors again prepare IAS individual accounts for the company, subsections (3) and (4) apply again as if the first financial year for which such accounts are again prepared were the first IAS year.
@ref s 395(5) Again preparing IAS individual accounts after a change (src:5110)
GIVEN `the directors have changed to preparing Companies Act individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors again prepare IAS individual accounts for the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(5) subsections (3) and (4) apply again with the year of the new IAS accounts as the first IAS year` MEANS
    IF `the directors have changed to preparing Companies Act individual accounts` AND `the directors again prepare IAS individual accounts for the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, having changed to preparing Companies Act individual accounts, the directors again prepare IAS individual accounts for the company, subsections (3) and (4) apply again"

-- ---- s 396, s 397: what the individual accounts must state and comprise ----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5112 | (A1) Companies Act individual accounts must state—
-- src:5113 | (a) the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered,
-- src:5114 | (b) the company’s registered number,
-- src:5115 | (c) whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee,
-- src:5116 | (d) the address of the company’s registered office, and
-- src:5117 | (e) where appropriate, the fact that the company is being wound-up.
@ref s 396(A1) What Companies Act individual accounts must state (src:5112-5117)
GIVEN `the accounts state the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state the company's registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state the address of the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state that the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(A1) the accounts state what subsection (A1) requires` MEANS
    IF `the accounts state the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered` AND `the accounts state the company's registered number` AND `the accounts state whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee` AND `the accounts state the address of the company's registered office` AND ((NOT `the company is being wound up`) OR `the accounts state that the company is being wound up`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Companies Act individual accounts must state— (a) the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered"

-- src:5118 | (1) Companies Act individual accounts must comprise—
-- src:5119 | (a) a balance sheet as at the last day of the financial year, and
-- src:5120 | (b) a profit and loss account.
@ref s 396(1) What Companies Act individual accounts must comprise (src:5118-5120)
GIVEN `the accounts comprise a balance sheet as at the last day of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts comprise a profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(1) the accounts comprise what subsection (1) requires` MEANS
    IF `the accounts comprise a balance sheet as at the last day of the financial year` AND `the accounts comprise a profit and loss account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Companies Act individual accounts must comprise— (a) a balance sheet as at the last day of the financial year, and (b) a profit and loss account"

-- src:5121 | (2) The accounts must—
-- src:5122 | (a) in the case of the balance sheet, give a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year, and
-- src:5123 | (b) in the case of the profit and loss account, give a true and fair view of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year.
@ref s 396(2) The true and fair view of the balance sheet and the profit and loss account (src:5121-5123)
GIVEN `the balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(2) the accounts give the true and fair view subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year` AND `the profit and loss account gives a true and fair view of the profit or loss of the company for the financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accounts must— (a) in the case of the balance sheet, give a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the company as at the end of the financial year"

-- src:5124 | (2A) In the case of the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year (see sections 384A and 384B), the micro-entity minimum accounting items included in the company’s accounts for the year are presumed to give the true and fair view required by subsection (2).
@ref s 396(2A) Micro-entities: the minimum accounting items are presumed to give the true and fair view (src:5124)
GIVEN `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts include the micro-entity minimum accounting items` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(2A) the micro-entity minimum accounting items are presumed to give the true and fair view required by subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the company qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year` AND `the accounts include the micro-entity minimum accounting items`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of the individual accounts of a company which qualifies as a micro-entity in relation to the financial year"

-- src:5125 | (3) The accounts must comply with provision made by the Secretary of State by regulations as to—
-- src:5126 | (a) the form and content of the balance sheet and profit and loss account, and
-- src:5127 | (b) additional information to be provided by way of notes to the accounts.
@ref s 396(3) Compliance with the Secretary of State's regulations (src:5125-5127)
-- The regulations are not among the sources: whether the accounts comply with them is a plain input.
GIVEN `the accounts comply with the regulations as to the form and content of the balance sheet and profit and loss account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts comply with the regulations as to additional information to be provided by way of notes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(3) the accounts comply with the regulations subsection (3) refers to` MEANS
    IF `the accounts comply with the regulations as to the form and content of the balance sheet and profit and loss account` AND `the accounts comply with the regulations as to additional information to be provided by way of notes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accounts must comply with provision made by the Secretary of State by regulations as to"

-- src:5131 | (6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not apply in relation to the micro-entity minimum accounting items included in the individual accounts of a company for a financial year in relation to which the company qualifies as a micro-entity.
@ref s 396(6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not apply to the micro-entity minimum accounting items (src:5131)
GIVEN `the item is a micro-entity minimum accounting item included in the individual accounts of a company for a financial year in relation to which the company qualifies as a micro-entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply to the item` MEANS
    IF `the item is a micro-entity minimum accounting item included in the individual accounts of a company for a financial year in relation to which the company qualifies as a micro-entity`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (4) and (5) do not apply in relation to the micro-entity minimum accounting items included in the individual accounts of a company for a financial year in relation to which the company qualifies as a micro-entity"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only takes the micro-entity minimum accounting items out of subsections (4) and (5)

-- src:5128 | (4) If compliance with the regulations, and any other provision made by or under this Act as to the matters to be included in a company's individual accounts or in notes to those accounts, would not be sufficient to give a true and fair view, the necessary additional information must be given in the accounts or in a note to them.
@ref s 396(4) Additional information where compliance would not be sufficient for a true and fair view (src:5128)
GIVEN `compliance with the regulations, and any other provision made by or under this Act as to the matters to be included in the accounts or notes, would not be sufficient to give a true and fair view` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 396(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply to the item` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(4) the necessary additional information must be given in the accounts or in a note` MEANS
    IF `s 396(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply to the item` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (4) and (5) do not apply in relation to the micro-entity minimum accounting items"
    ELSE IF `compliance with the regulations, and any other provision made by or under this Act as to the matters to be included in the accounts or notes, would not be sufficient to give a true and fair view`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If compliance with the regulations, and any other provision made by or under this Act as to the matters to be included in a company's individual accounts or in notes to those accounts, would not be sufficient to give a true and fair view, the necessary additional information must be given"

-- src:5129 | (5) If in special circumstances compliance with any of those provisions is inconsistent with the requirement to give a true and fair view, the directors must depart from that provision to the extent necessary to give a true and fair view.
-- src:5130 | Particulars of any such departure, the reasons for it and its effect must be given in a note to the accounts.
@ref s 396(5) Departure from a provision where compliance is inconsistent with a true and fair view (src:5129-5130)
GIVEN `in special circumstances compliance with any of those provisions is inconsistent with the requirement to give a true and fair view` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 396(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply to the item` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(5) the directors must depart from the provision to the extent necessary, and give particulars in a note` MEANS
    IF `s 396(6) subsections (4) and (5) apply to the item` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (4) and (5) do not apply in relation to the micro-entity minimum accounting items"
    ELSE IF `in special circumstances compliance with any of those provisions is inconsistent with the requirement to give a true and fair view`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in special circumstances compliance with any of those provisions is inconsistent with the requirement to give a true and fair view, the directors must depart from that provision"

-- src:5133 | (1) IAS individual accounts must state—
-- src:5134 | (a) the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered,
-- src:5135 | (b) the company’s registered number,
-- src:5136 | (c) whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee,
-- src:5137 | (d) the address of the company’s registered office, and
-- src:5138 | (e) where appropriate, the fact that the company is being wound-up.
@ref s 397(1) What IAS individual accounts must state (src:5133-5138)
GIVEN `the accounts state the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state the company's registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state the address of the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts state that the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(1) the IAS individual accounts state what subsection (1) requires` MEANS
    -- the five statements are the same as those of s 396(A1) in the text of both sections
    `s 396(A1) the accounts state what subsection (A1) requires` `the accounts state the part of the United Kingdom in which the company is registered` `the accounts state the company's registered number` `the accounts state whether the company is a public or a private company and whether it is limited by shares or by guarantee` `the accounts state the address of the company's registered office` `the company is being wound up` `the accounts state that the company is being wound up`

-- src:5139 | (2) The notes to the accounts must state that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards.
@ref s 397(2) The notes must state that the accounts follow UK-adopted international accounting standards (src:5139)
GIVEN `the notes to the accounts state that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 397(2) the notes state that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards` MEANS
    IF `the notes to the accounts state that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notes to the accounts must state that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards"

